  "title": "Promise: Amend the National Health Act to increase funding for the Basic Health Care Provision Fund (BHCPF) from 1% to at least 2% of the Consolidated Revenue Fund to tackle prevalent deficiencies in healthcare resources and infrastructure.",
  "source": "https://placng.org/i/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Legislative-Agenda-of-the-10th-House-of-Representatives.pdf",
  "subject_area": "healthcare",
  "promise_blog": "<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;10&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\" data-doc-id=\"2500059000000810050\" data-doc-type=\"writer\"><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">In its Legislative Agenda document, the 10th Assembly of the House of Representatives prioritises health and pledged to address the funding problem in the health sector by increasing funding for the Basic Health Care Provision Fund (BHCPF). The legislators through lawmaking promised to amend the National Health Act, especially the section that focused on the Consolidated Revenue Fund.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;10&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\" data-doc-id=\"2500059000000810050\" data-doc-type=\"writer\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;9.75&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\"><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">The Basic Health Care Provision Fund (BHCPF) was established under section 11 of the National Health Act as a catalytic funding to improve access to primary health care. According to the information on the national Primary Health Care Development Agency (NPHCDA) <a href=\"https://nphcda.gov.ng/bhcpf/\">website</a>, \"the BHCPF serves to fund Basic Minimum Package of Health Services (BMPHS), increase the fiscal space for health, strengthen the national health system particularly at primary health care (PHC) level by making provision for routine daily operation cost of PHCs, and ensure access to health care for all, particularly the poor, thus contributing to overall national productivity.\"</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(0, 0, 0)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;9.75&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(68, 68, 68)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;10&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\"><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">Currently, the country is witnessing an increasing demand for quality health care despite numerous challenges in making it accessible to all. In its 2023 National Health Facility Survey (NHFS), the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) <a href=\"https://nairametrics.com/2024/12/22/no-region-in-nigeria-has-50-access-to-functional-basic-medical-equipment-nbs-report/\">revealed</a> that no region in Nigeria has 50% access to the functional basic medical equipment in health facilities.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(68, 68, 68)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;10&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(68, 68, 68)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;12.00&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\"><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">However, the implementation of BHCPF has reaped tangible results as the sector continue to grapple with intense challenges. According to the Coordinating Minister for Health, Prof. Muhammed Ali Pate, the BHCPF-funded primary health care facilities have been <a href=\"https://dailytrust.com/over-10m-nigerians-accessing-care-under-basic-health-care-provision-fund-fg/\">extended</a> to over 10 million Nigerians who he said are receiving health care services through the fund.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"zw-paragraph\" data-textformat=\"{&quot;ff&quot;:&quot;Arimo&quot;,&quot;fv&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;td&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;cs&quot;:&quot;0pt&quot;,&quot;fw&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;fgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(68, 68, 68)&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;12.00&quot;,&quot;va&quot;:&quot;baseline&quot;,&quot;fw_i&quot;:500,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;fs&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;bgc&quot;:&quot;rgb(255, 255, 255)&quot;}\" data-margin-bottom=\"12pt\" data-line-height=\"1.2\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">The fulfilment of this pledge will mean an increase in funding for the health sector and a solid commitment to the tackling of the prevalent deficiencies in healthcare resources and infrastructure.</span></p>",
