    "blog": "<h1><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Funding for Basic Health Care Provision Fund Yet to Increase</strong></span></h1>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;\">The promise by the Rt. Hon. Tajudeen Abbas-led House of Representatives to increase the funding for the Basic Health Care Provision Fund (BHCPF) from 1% to 2% per cent of the consoliadated Revenue Fund through the amendment of the National Health Act (NHA) is yet to materialise.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">As at June 11, 2025, the amendment bill for the NHA currently under consideration by the legislators is yet to be presented for third reading. Therefore, we rate this promise Broken.</span></p>",
